    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1c031b5_c41a6c7f",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 1143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-20T01:03:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t necessarily need to update ROLLBACK for every release (neither should we: it makes recovery to an older image harder). The idea is only to increment it if we know a previous version is compromised.",
      "parentUuid": "65cbb7f4_f729f9ff",
      "revId": "ca0e82685989a08c6adaa52fc8d33546cd3bb1a2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0836c5a_a80ddbef",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 1143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-20T02:29:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Got it, but using unix timestamp is also a good idea too, then we don\u0027t have to worry about increment the value at all.",
      "parentUuid": "a1c031b5_c41a6c7f",
      "revId": "ca0e82685989a08c6adaa52fc8d33546cd3bb1a2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6a4dcb8_c64d633f",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 1143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-20T02:35:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should always increment ROLLBACK. As I said it makes recovery to an older image harder.\n\ne.g. if you have rootfs B on dev channel, with FW b, and something does not work (e.g. new trackpad FW is broken, or rootfs is too buggy), you want to be able to downgrade to rootfs A on stable channel, and flash back FW a (so you get back the \"known good\" old FW, and in some cases it might be that fw b isn\u0027t compatible with rootfs A).\n\nROLLBACK uprev should only be used exceptionally (just like the AP FW rollback protection, we use that very rarely).",
      "parentUuid": "e0836c5a_a80ddbef",
      "revId": "ca0e82685989a08c6adaa52fc8d33546cd3bb1a2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
